          "at": "2026-09-07T12:31:08Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "path normalization",
              "file": "apps/cli-driver/src/track_resolution.rs",
              "line": 61,
              "message": "`current_dir().join(value)` produces only a lexical absolute path and leaves components such as `.` intact. The default `.` therefore becomes `<cwd>/.`, which does not prefix-match Cargo's `<cwd>/target` in the downstream path comparisons, so target exclusion can still fail. Canonicalize the existing directory (with fail-closed error handling) before storing it.",
              "severity": "high"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:6f5e96ed10d9dd1299c12df4e002606c4a349c736663078d152ecca0eb260f8b",
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "findings_remain"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-09-07T12:41:12Z",
          "findings": [],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:909288dc0c322fb34aaa59fc46c8ceb702d83ad2eea636041225f3032b449894",
          "type": "fast",
          "verdict": "zero_findings"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-09-07T13:03:06Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "boundary validation",
              "file": "apps/cli-driver/src/track_resolution.rs",
              "line": 99,
              "message": "`TrackWorkspaceRootInput` can still be constructed without the new normalization invariant. `from_derived_items_parent` stores its argument directly, and both public `TrackItemsDirectoryInput::workspace_root` methods reach this unchecked path (the resolution variant constructs the struct directly). A relative or missing `track/items` input can therefore produce a relative or unavailable workspace root that `catalogue_impl_signals_input_to_command` forwards after only lexical use-case validation, recreating the relative/absolute target-exclusion failure. Route derived roots through the new fallible normalization and propagate its diagnostic, or remove the unchecked construction path.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
          "hash": "rvw1:sha256:909288dc0c322fb34aaa59fc46c8ceb702d83ad2eea636041225f3032b449894",
          "type": "final",
          "verdict": "findings_remain"
        },
        {
          "at": "2026-09-07T13:25:45Z",
          "findings": [
            {
              "category": "boundary validation",
              "file": "apps/cli-driver/src/track_resolution.rs",
              "line": 99,
              "message": "`TrackWorkspaceRootInput` still has construction paths that bypass the new normalization invariant. `from_derived_items_parent` stores its argument directly; `track_tddd::TrackItemsDirectoryInput::workspace_root` calls it, and the resolution-layer `TrackItemsDirectoryInput::workspace_root` likewise constructs the value directly. A relative or unavailable `track/items` path can therefore yield a relative/unavailable workspace root that `catalogue_impl_signals_input_to_command` forwards after only lexical validation, recreating the target-exclusion failure. Route derived roots through the fallible normalization and propagate its diagnostic, or prevent unchecked construction.",
              "severity": "P1"
            }
          ],
